  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance for Ethiopia, Kenya, Somalia and Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment has provided humanitarian funding in response to  humanitarian need across the Greater Horn of Africa focusing on disability, gender, and nutrition. The investment focuses on assistance and protection ensuring that affected populations have equitable access to quality protection and humanitarian assistance. In 2022 &#x2013; 2024, DFAT funded multilateral partners and Australian Humanitarian Partnership (AHP) organisations through agreements focused on operations in Ethiopia, Kenya, Somalia and Sudan. The multilateral partners include; United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees, United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs, International Committee of the Red Cross, World Food Programme, Emergency Action Alliance, World Vision, OXFAM and Plan International.</narrative>
  </description>
